WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280
Let's warm up with Russian words for snow, ice, and weather that will help you chat about chilly days. I'm Olya, and this is

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:14.420
привет, Русский, episode 78. Our word of the day is snow, snow, say it with me, snow, it means snow.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:21.740
Think of the soft sounds, snow makes when it lands, like a quites, snow is that covers everything in white. Here is a simple sentence,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:28.020
Сняк белый, снег белый, да snow is white, репита в торми, снег, снег.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.000
Now we add more winter words that go with снег.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.640
The next word is лед, лед, it means ice, лед rhymes with load, and you can picture a heavy

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.140
load of slippery ice on the ground, say it slowly, лед.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.940
The ice feels cold, so we say, лед холодный, лед холодный, the ice is cold.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.760
Некст – камс дождь.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:49.220
Дождь.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:50.740
Доса-сворт – Минз Рейн.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.440
Ит-сам – забит лэк-дождь.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.200
Но это бренкс-воттер из «Доска» в СТЕДУ в МЕДЕССН.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.460
Репит авторми.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.200
Дождь.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.080
Дождь идет.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:00:59.160
Дождь идет.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.380
Это Зрейнин.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.900
Ветер камс-некст.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.420
Ветер – It means wind.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.420
Ветер – it is like better weather when a cool breeze helps on a warm day.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:08.600
Сэйт в ДМИ.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.300
Ветер.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.440
Ветер дует.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.560
Ветер дует.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.840
The wind is blowing.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.140
The sun often appears even in winter.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:22.160
и its word is sun-то, sun-то, it means sun, sun-то starts like solar, our big sun is star in the sky,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.860
repeat after me, sun-то, sun-то светит, sun-то светит, the sun is shining,

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:33.800
two useful phrases tell us how the air feels, холодно, холодно, this means it is cold,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.560
холодно feels like cold with a Russian ending, say it slowly, холодно,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.480
Сегодня холодно, сегодня холодно, it is cold today.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.140
The opposite is тепло, тепло, it means it is warm.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.760
тепло sounds like tapet, but means nicely warm in Koji.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:55.440
Repita вторми, тепло, в доме тепло, в доме тепло, it is warm in the house.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.960
Our last word is zima, zima, it means winter.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.780
Zima carries a sense of zil for building snowmen and playing outside.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.580
Say it with me, zima.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:10.660
Зима холодная, зима холодная, Winter is cold, Russian adjectives change their endings

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.120
to match the noun they describe.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.440
Take холодный, холодный, it means cold and works with masculine words like ветер.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.720
When the noun is feminine, like Zima, the ending becomes холодная, холодная.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.920
This agreement makes the sentence sound natural, unlike English, where the adjective stays

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.340
the same no matter the noun.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:36.120
Рашенсован старт конверсейсions by mentioning the weather, because winter is last a long time and bring plenty of snow.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:44.640
A friendly phrase you can try is «какой холод» – «какой холод» – it means what cold and works well on a snowy street.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:50.340
For our practice time, kids can draw a snowy scene and label the snow like snow and snow.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.520
Then say each word out loud.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:58.620
Adults look out the window and make one simple sentence about today's weather using two new words,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.240
сейчас сегодня холодно и снег.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.480
Before we finish, here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.940
Zima began long ago in an early Slavic form that shares an ancient route with the Sanskrit

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.460
word Hima, for snow or frost.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.620
That same route gave the Himalayas their name, the abode of snow.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.640
The word travelled through early Slavic languages and kept almost the same sound in Russian.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.720
A playful false friend appears in some other languages, where a similar sound means

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.800
«Earth instead of a season».

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.360
Пикчера химолайн-пик, Каворта Невер-Мелтинг-земас-Но,

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.400
ту локда-коннекшена Нью-Рмайнд.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:36.260
Молодец!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.360
Сегодня вы выучили новое слова.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.000
Скажите их в слух еще раз медленно и спокойно.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.100
До встречи в следующем уроке.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:44.760
Пока!

